<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>false</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1707</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Clean Architecture (constitution Art. IV.2) — status of enforcement, stated accurately:

    The TARGET is that a `.Domain` project references no framework, no EF Core and no Supabase SDK.
    As of the first vertical slice there are NO Domain projects and NO architecture tests, so
    nothing enforces it yet: the rule is a convention in the documentation, not a build guard.

    It becomes a guarantee when the first domain module lands, by pairing "(a) a project that
    references only the base class library" with "(b) a NetArchTest architecture test". Until then
    this comment must not claim enforcement it does not have — a false guarantee in a build file is
    worse than none, because reviewers stop checking.
  -->

</Project>
